US EPA, Office of Water. Understanding Water Treatment Chemical Supply Chains and the Risk of Disruptions. [Official report and context](https://www.epa.gov/waterutilityresponse/risk-disruptions-supply-water-treatment-chemicals) · [Complete 61-file-page report](https://www.epa.gov/system/files/documents/2023-03/Understanding%20Water%20Treatment%20Chemical%20Supply%20Chains%20and%20the%20Risk%20of%20Disruptions.pdf).

Read the whole report and reconstruct its methodology and case evidence. Use it as a substantial dated study of chemical dependence, precursors, competing demand and disruption, then test how a particular user's circumstances differ from national aggregates.

